          "overview": "Session d02 discusses only paper 2004.00809, \"Mapping Languages and Demographics with Georeferenced Corpora\" — first and last cited. Across five evidence-checking turns (t4–t8) the recurring question was why Twitter data better predicts each country's language inventory. Evidence confirmed the abstract claim, fewer missing languages, better North America/Oceania representation, r=0.60 vs r=0.49, and candidate explanations (GDP-weighted wealthier population, urban-centered collection, English/Spanish commonness), with no direct causal test. Unresolved references: no explicit mechanism for the inventory advantage; open questions on false-positive sources (immigration, tourism, business; Russia case) and whether rural-centered collection yields the same bias.",
